    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0573" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3331/365a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-11T00:00:00-04:00">May 11,
                        1941—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Please advise Uruguayan authorities that the press releases in regard to
                    public notices of intention to negotiate with Uruguay and Argentina will be
                    released for publication in papers appearing on the streets after 9 p.m. E. S.
                    T. May 12.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d468-f1"/> The draft releases, which are
                    routine in nature, refer to the public notices issued by the Secretary of State
                    and by the Committee for Reciprocity Information in regard to briefs and public
                    hearings and to the lists of products on which the United States will consider
                    granting concessions.</p>
                <p>Please acknowledge receipt of this telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
